PURPOSE of misc/wait-guest-poweroff
Description: Wait for guest poweroff
Author: Erico Nunes <ernunes@redhat.com>

Wait for guest poweroff.

This is intended to be used by the Host in a Beaker job using a
<guestrecipe>.
When using it, the Host machine waits for the guest machine to power off
to have a chance to safely modify the guest settings (such as VM
configuration, firmware settings).
The Host should then power it back on in a separate further task.

See also: misc/self-poweroff
